From d9860d5c2b2e5c8c0e77942ca76f16c6f02da4d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atjiki1 <atjiki1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:43:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] bt: keep a secondary BLE bonding next to the phone

With CONFIG_BT_MULTI_LINK_EXPERIMENT, store up to one gateway (phone)
and one secondary BLE bonding instead of a single one:

- a new pairing made while secondary pairing is active and a gateway
  bonding exists is stored with is_gateway = supports_ancs = false
- an updated bonding keeps its existing role
- adding a bonding only replaces older bondings with the same role,
  also when pruning at boot
- deleting the secondary leaves the PRF copy of the gateway alone
- the secondary identity is cached in RAM, so it can be checked with
  bt_lock() held

Secondary pairing is set by the Bluetooth settings menu through
bt_pairability_set_secondary_pairing().

Assisted-by: LLM
